  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "| | Presente simple | Presente continuo |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **Cuándo** | rutinas, hábitos, hechos permanentes | ahora, algo temporal o que está en curso |",
      "| **Forma** | sujeto + verbo (he **works**) · do/does + verbo en preguntas | **am / is / are + verbo-ing** |",
      "| **Palabras** | always, usually, often, sometimes, never, every day, on Mondays | now, at the moment, today, this week, currently |",
      "| **Ejemplo** | *I usually work in the office.* | *I'm working from home this week.* |",
      "",
      "**Preguntas:** *Do you work from home? — No, I don't.* · *What are you doing? — I'm writing a report.*",
      "",
      "**Verbos de estado (casi nunca en continuo):** *know, like, love, hate, want, need, understand, believe, prefer, have (poseer)*. → *I know the answer.* (no *I'm knowing*) · *I want a coffee.* (no *I'm wanting*).",
      "",
      "**Ortografía de -ing:** *write → writing · sit → sitting · run → running · work → working*.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *usually* /ˈjuːʒuəli/ (la -s- suena /ʒ/)."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I'm knowing the answer.",
        "right": "I know the answer.",
        "note": "Los verbos de estado no se usan en continuo."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I work from home this week.",
        "right": "I'm working from home this week.",
        "note": "Algo temporal: presente continuo."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
